{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c35c7b26-ede3-4b86-a35a-98794e30e1e9","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\n  \"doc_id\": \"seeded_lms\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-005\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall lock a Member account after 5 consecutive failed login attempts within a 10-minute window\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies locking the account after 5 consecutive failed logins, but omits the lockout duration, unlock/recovery procedure, and user notification or error response.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-006\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"notify him\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The pronoun 'him' has multiple plausible antecedents (the Librarian, the Member, or the Guarantor), making the intended email recipient ambiguous.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-007\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD minutes\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the placeholder 'TBD' instead of specifying the exact password-reset token expiration duration in minutes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-008\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"user-friendly; easy to navigate; loads rapidly; standard connections\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Relies on subjective, unquantified terms ('user-friendly', 'easy to navigate', 'loads rapidly', 'standard connections') without measurable usability, latency, or bandwidth criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-012\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at most TBD consecutive times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the placeholder 'TBD' instead of defining the exact maximum number of consecutive loan renewals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall validate item eligibility within 2 seconds and issue the loan receipt\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes only the happy path for self-checkout barcode validation and receipt issuance without specifying system behavior when the barcode is invalid or the item is ineligible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the allowed maximum number of active hold requests\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"References a numeric cap ('the allowed maximum number of active hold requests') without specifying the actual limit value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-009\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Permits a Member in good standing to borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously, contradicting SD-009, which limits simultaneous checkouts to at most 5 physical items.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-016\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"21 calendar days from the checkout timestamp\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-010\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Sets the standard loan period for circulating print books to 21 calendar days, conflicting with SD-010, which sets it to 14 calendar days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-017\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Unverified visitors shall be able to self-register online with only an email address and immediately check out physical books without Librarian ID verification\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Allows unverified self-registration with only an email address and immediate book checkout without ID verification, directly contradicting SD-001, which requires a Librarian to verify government-issued photo ID and record full name, email, and phone number before account creation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-018\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall remain held indefinitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-011\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires reserved items on the pickup shelf to be held indefinitely until manually cancelled by the Member, contradicting SD-011, which mandates automatic hold cancellation after 72 hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses chained 'and/or' connectives, leaving it ambiguous which exact combination of the three actions must be executed when an item is 7 days overdue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without identifying which role or system component is responsible for reviewing, approving, and recording overdue fine waiver requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The non-binding qualifier 'if appropriate' leaves the conditions for dispatching SMS due-date alerts subjective and unverifiable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the placeholder 'TBD' instead of specifying the exact retention period in years for payment receipts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap on accumulated fines\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies an overdue fine of $1.25 USD per day with no maximum cap, contradicting SD-019, which sets the fine at $0.50 USD per day capped at $20.00 USD per item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-020\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Permits Members to renew borrowed items regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance, contradicting SD-020, which blocks renewals whenever a Member's unpaid fine balance exceeds $5.00 USD.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Patron's active loan count; Patron profile screen\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\",\n        \"SD-009\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Introduces the term 'Patron' for the library borrower role instead of the established term 'Member' used in SD-001, SD-009, and across earlier requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"quickly; many users\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms 'quickly' and 'many users' without specifying a maximum response time or concurrent user load.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The loophole qualifier 'where possible' makes query term highlighting optional and lacks testable criteria for when highlighting is required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient ISBN matching accuracy; acceptable response times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective terms 'sufficient' and 'acceptable' without defining measurable accuracy percentages or latency thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently; large batch MARC21 files; noticeable system slowdown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms ('efficiently', 'large', 'noticeable') without specifying throughput, file size/record count, or allowable performance degradation bounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only that the Catalog Service detects active loans or holds on a deletion attempt, without stating the resulting action (e.g., blocking deletion and returning an error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the placeholder 'TBD' instead of specifying the exact scheduled interval for encrypted full database backups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important administrative actions; in a timely manner; an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective, unquantified phrases ('important', 'in a timely manner', 'an appropriate period') without enumerating the audited actions, logging latency, or retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Triggers logging FAILOVER-01 when the primary database node is unreachable for over 10 seconds, but omits the actual failover, recovery, or traffic-rerouting behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate transport security; clear error messages\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective terms 'adequate' and 'clear' without specifying concrete transport security standards (e.g., TLS version) or testable error message criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"accept any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Accepts any Member password of at least 8 characters, conflicting with SD-002, which requires at least 12 characters containing uppercase, lowercase, and numeric characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Keeps web portal sessions active for 60 minutes of user inactivity, conflicting with SD-004, which terminates sessions after 15 minutes of inactivity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so Administrators can decrypt and retrieve forgotten passwords upon request\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires reversible AES-256 encryption of Member passwords so Administrators can decrypt them, directly contradicting SD-003, which mandates one-way bcrypt hashing (cost factor 12) and prohibits storing or retrieving plaintext passwords.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":129.149687,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":15098,"output_tokens":16791,"thinking_tokens":13483,"cache_read_tokens":12930,"total_tokens":31889}}}
